[[0,1379433,0,2,0,2,"2016-10-31T03:08:43","Joe_McCarthy","",[],"","Geert Wilders boycotts race hate trial","http://www.theaustralian.com.au/news/world/the-times/geert-wilders-boycotts-race-hate-trial/news-story/0ba68f2db650657f5f5ca23bc5540915","OccidentalEnclave"],[1,6693926,0,4,0,4,"2016-10-31T03:19:26","ratsmack","",[],"<p>Subscriber only article - you'll have to post a summary as it can't be archived.</p>"],[2,6694066,6693926,3,0,3,"2016-10-31T03:46:08","Joe_McCarthy","",[],"<p><a href=\"https://www.yahoo.com/news/dutch-far-leader-wilders-trial-inciting-hatred-233309837.html\">https://www.yahoo.com/news/dutch-far-leader-wilders-trial-inciting-hatred-233309837.html</a></p>"],[1,6695282,0,2,0,2,"2016-10-31T10:22:10","Quaestorr","",[],"<p>It was expected he'd be using court as a stage, but he made it known he won't attend.</p>\n<p>I don't know what to think of Wilders nowadays... He has been a great catalyst of the emerging anti-immigration and anti-multiculturalism sentiment, but he's also somewhat of a hindrance in not cooperating with anyone, and not letting the phenomenon grow bigger. I don't think Wilders ever read Evola, but he seems like he likes to 'live in the antithesis' — and wants to remain there.</p>\n<p>It doesn't seem like his party would be able to participate in a new administration. I presume Bosma and Fritsma are capable, but I am simply not under the impression that there is something like an 'inner party' or even an informal team. It should also be noted that Wilders' political party only has one member: Geert Wilders. All the other people are employees or volunteers, but not members.</p>\n<p>So most of the seats the PVV holds in the parliament, are occupied by nobodies (Wilders doesn't even have the time or the opportunity —he's still heavily guarded by the Dutch national security agency and moved from one hidden location to the other— to talk to the people who are on the top of list, and I presume he might have talked to those in the lower echelons only during their application interview). But I suppose that even that is better than having the seats occupied by the nobodies of some pro-immigration party.</p>"]]
